Usage: sed [OPTION]... {script} [FILE]...

Apply basic sed scripts (s///, p, d, a, i, c) to each line of input.

OPTIONS:
  -n, --quiet            suppress automatic printing of pattern space
      --silent           alias for -n
  -s, --separate         consider files as separate rather than as a single
                         continuous long stream
  -z, --null-data        separate lines by NUL characters
      --zero-terminated  alias for -z
  -u, --unbuffered       buffer input and output minimally
  -b, --binary           open files in binary mode
  -i, --in-place[=ARG]   edit files in place
  -e, --expression ARG   add the script to the commands to be executed
  -f, --file ARG         add the script from FILE
  -l, --line-length NUM  specify line-wrap length for the l command
  -E, --regexp-extended  use extended regular expressions
      --debug            annotate program execution (accepted, no output)
      --follow-symlinks  follow symlinks when processing in place (accepted,
                         no-op)
      --sandbox          restrict file system access in the script
      --posix            disable GNU extensions and follow POSIX sed
  -r                     alias for -E
      --help             display this help and exit
  -V, --version          output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
